    "title": "Fix discard and explore defects exposed by Industrial produced-token qualification",
    "user": {
      "login": "GodaPupa",
      "id": 326515697,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOE3Y78Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/326515697?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/GodaPupa",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/GodaPupa/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "The produced Blood/Map qualification at 8f8ec082 failed 4 of 18 focused cases and exposed two engine defects: nonrandom discard costs could move a foreign or otherwise ineligible hand card, and exploring an empty library omitted the required counter. This successor validates the selected discard prefix before movement and reuses the existing explore counter helper. Two Map fixtures now submit the actual YesNo decision; all original names and outcome assertions remain intact.\n\nThe generic fixes are shared engine changes. No card definition, deck, pilot, protocol, seed, allocation or gameplay permission changes. Two generic regressions cover duplicate selection and filter enforcement. Qualification prospectively requires 20 focused cases and 154 broader card/status cases; the focused cases overlap that broader bank. Full CI and the required shared receiving/runtime gates still require actual source-bound artifacts and independent review.\n\nThe repository's add-feature Step8a is applied conservatively: the workflow also runs the prescribed VOW and LCI Assay differentials, retains complete rows and exit codes, proves the parser/SDK/golden inputs are unchanged from the failed source, and preserves the actual relevant Oracle reference rows plus whole-bulk hashes. Divergent rows require classification; no snapshot or parser result is automatically adopted.\n\nThe original failed attempt remains durable at receiving-evidence commit be3e2b43acb6ddcea9ac7ff289821329707a8077, under `industrial-waste/v2/evidence/produced-token-attempt-01-source-8f8ec082/`. Its broader 152-case step did not execute. The original failure is not retroactively changed by this repair. Existing 94af/e5 runtime acceptance cannot transfer to the changed engine source.\n\nIndependent source and dependency reviews are bounded publication/qualification reviews, not GitHub approval, complete-runtime admission or authority to execute the 512-allocation R1 corpus. Official execution remains 0/512.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-26T23:14:05Z",
